Task: Implement PaymentEventConsumer + Main wiring (US-6.3 Phase 2)

Summary: Added PaymentEventConsumer.scala, mirroring StockEventConsumer.scala's
structure exactly:
- PaymentSettledEvent/PaymentFailedEvent local mirrors (orderId, paymentId,
  amountCents, timestamp), circe Codec via deriveCodec.
- settledStream (consumer group order-service-payment-settled, topic
  payment.settled) and failedStream (group order-service-payment-failed,
  topic payment.failed), each: decode -> on failure log+commit-skip; on
  success call store.updateStatusIfCurrent(orderId, Reserved, target),
  publish order.status-changed via the existing OrderEventPublisher on
  Some, log outcome, commit offset regardless.
- run[F] merges both streams, same signature shape as StockEventConsumer.run.
- Main.scala: StockEventConsumer.run merged with PaymentEventConsumer.run
  before compiling/draining/backgrounding as one fiber, sharing the same
  OrderEventPublisher instance built earlier in the resource chain.

Tests (PaymentEventConsumerSuite.scala, new, 8 tests):
- payment.settled -> Confirmed transition
- payment.failed -> PaymentFailed transition
- non-Reserved order (still Pending) -> no-op, doesn't block a later real event
- unknown orderId -> no-op, doesn't block a later real event
- malformed JSON -> decode-failure no-op, doesn't block a later real event
- cross-topic routing: settled and failed events for two different orders
  each land on their own distinct target status, not the other's
- payment.settled also publishes order.status-changed (status=confirmed,
  correct orderId/customerId)
- payment.failed also publishes order.status-changed (status=payment_failed)

Applied the US-5.3/US-5.4 lesson proactively: used consumeMatching
(filter by order id) from the start instead of consumeOne, since this
suite's tests share one Testcontainers Kafka instance and can run with a
real (non-noOp) publisher concurrently - confirmed stable across 3 repeated
runs (8/8 each time).

Files changed:
- src/main/scala/orderservice/PaymentEventConsumer.scala (new)
- src/test/scala/orderservice/PaymentEventConsumerSuite.scala (new)
- src/main/scala/orderservice/Main.scala

Verification: 133/133 tests pass (full suite). Coverage: 92.42% statement /
92.62% branch overall.

Why: closes Phase 4's order-service side - once payment-service settles or
fails a charge, the order now actually reaches confirmed/payment_failed and
notification-service (US-7.1, separate repo) has an order.status-changed
event to react to.
